  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 311 PM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nUpper level low pressure will transition east along the \nMontana/Canadian border Sunday. The severe threat should shift \nnorth into the western and central Dakotas Sunday night. \nHowever, we may see a strong to severe storm along a trailing \nfrontal boundary. This feature will track across the forecast \narea Sunday night so am expecting a \"late show\" across the \nforecast area with convection during the late evening to \novernight hours. Beyond Sunday, upper level high pressure will \ntransition east from the Arklatex into the Tennessee Valley. \nGulf moisture on the back side to the high will lift from the \nsouthern plains into eastern Kansas and the lower Missouri \nValley. The latest mid model solns indicate a drier airmass \nacross central and western Nebraska, leading to lower \nprecipitation chances across the area. This drier trend will \nbegin on Tuesday and continue into Friday next week. After highs\nin the 80s to near 90 for Monday and Tuesday, above normal \ntemperatures will arrive Wednesday continuing through Friday\nwith highs generally in the lower to mid 90s.",
